WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:31.289
This is a message for all the people.
This is a message from the future,

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:37.890
transmitted to its past. The moment
has come for all people to embrace new

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:45.390
ideas, to solve the most complex problem of all: the long-term survival of complex

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:51.390
life on the planet. This is a call for the 
people of Earth to become interplanetary.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:56.740
It is a plea for reflection.
It is a call to action.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:03.310
A request for reason. It is time to accept
the need to work towards the creation of

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:08.350
a prosperous Earth, and to bring the light of reason to the far reaches of the galaxy.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:15.970
This is a message for all people of Earth, and the descendents of earthlings.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:27.990
It is time to change the world one planet at a time.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:33.520
Let's face it: there's something crazy
and a bit epic about a project

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:37.500
whose tagline is, 
"Changing the world one planet at a time."

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:42.280
The whole idea of InterPlanetary grows out of complexity science.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:47.829
To be successful in a project like this you need very special people to ask crazy, ambitious questions...

00:01:47.829 --> 00:01:52.270
to be radical, maverick, and revolutionary. You know, one of the most important

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:56.140
photographs that we have is the photograph of the Earth from space, because what

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.549
that photograph showed us was this one
living planet in an otherwise lifeless universe.

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:04.179
And the fact is,
this planet won't last forever

00:02:04.179 --> 00:02:10.060
but we would like the best of what we
have created to last beyond our own planet.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.440
And to do this we need to combine so much of what
humans have created in their histories:

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:20.849
cities, civilizations, great works of art,
great works of music, scientific theories,

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:25.180
incredible artifacts of engineering –
we have to bring them all together.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:29.920
You have to set yourself an
almost impossible creative task.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.329
What would it take to become an interplanetary civilization?

00:02:34.329 --> 00:02:40.090
And everyone knows that when extraterrestrials visit the planet Earth
they crash in New Mexico.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.959
So why is InterPlanetary important now? One is, we're going through a new space race.

00:02:43.959 --> 00:02:47.950
There's huge interest on setting up a
colony on the Moon, building a colony on Mars...

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:51.519
There are clearly issues of
sustainable living and living with a purpose,

00:02:51.519 --> 00:02:56.810
and it's about the meaning of existence.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:03:01.870
We have to find a new language.
We need to find ways of allowing creative minds –

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:07.010
irrespective of privilege and economic
circumstance –&nbsp;to contribute to this project.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:11.270
We have the technology to do it.
We haven't had the cause –&nbsp;and that's

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:15.080
something that's motivating to everybody.
A festival like this, or a project like this,

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:20.030
can seem like a scientific question&nbsp;–&nbsp;
which it is –&nbsp;but beneath the science,

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:23.660
beneath the engineering, beneath the
technology, is one of the deepest

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:28.940
questions of all – and that is, "What is the ultimate objective of life in the universe?

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.700
What we're trying to do now is solve a

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:36.410
really hard cultural problem: we love
worlds that don't really exist.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:41.000
We in fact like worlds that don't really exist
more than the world that exists.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:47.420
We now turn to art, to film, or games, to
explore alternative ways of being but

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:51.739
what we want to do is take some of those
worlds that don't exist, and use them to

00:03:51.739 --> 00:03:57.350
improve the world that does exist.
And InterPlanetary takes our fascination

00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:03.260
in space, science fiction, rocketry, and it
combines it with new ideas and science

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:09.470
with a sense of urgency that we have to
change the way people think about the

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:14.720
complex system. Inject what we find in
science fiction, in literature, infuse it

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.100
back into rigorous ideas.
The lives individuals lead now

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:23.510
have consequences over the entire planet,
and so the InterPlanetary perspective

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:29.900
forces everybody to address the global
implications of their local behaviors.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:35.600
It's time to come together to solve a
huge problem. The problem is the problem of

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:39.770
the long-term sustainability of our planet 
and taking the best of what we've

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:44.270
done beyond the confines of our
atmosphere to the rest of the universe.

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:50.650
This is urgent. If we don't do this now,
we're f'ed beyond belief.

